{"failure_definitions":["Incapacitating fall (simulator fall and injury probabilities; base rate 0.15 per km is a team assumption).","Stored heat at or above 844 kJ (params.ts heatMaxKJ).","O2 exhausted, or below the 60-minute reserve on arrival.","With a solar storm active: not under cover when the shelter rule runs out (30 min from the alert, alert-to-first-step time included); when no open shelter can meet that rule any more, not under cover at the expected dose-rate peak (53 min after the alert).","Stuck (no legal move for 3 min) or not arrived after 3 h."],"assumptions":["Fall base rate 0.15 per km on easy ground: team assumption (Apollo fall counts have no distance denominator).","Chance that a fall is incapacitating 0.01 x (1 + v / 0.65) x 1.5 downhill, capped at 0.3: team assumption.","Suit cooling multiplier 1 - 0.117 z, floor 0.65 (380 W, NTRS 20160001058): assumed distribution.","Metabolic multiplier exp(0.12 z), x0.70 to x1.43: assumed distribution.","Navigation offset sigma 53 m (3 sigma = 160 m, JETT3 mean position error), fading out in the last 200 m: assumed distribution.","Pace drift exp(0.08 z) per 10 s step: assumed distribution.","All z are standard normal, clipped to +/-3. Robustness in nats is a likelihood ratio under these assumed distributions, not a probability.","Model-based results from one walk model on one site; not crew-validated."],"wording":"Adaptive Stress Testing (Lee et al., 2020) uses reinforcement learning to search a simulator for the most likely failure. We apply it to a physics-based walk model with documented bounds. Results are model-based, not crew-validated.","generated_utc":"2026-11-15T02:37:14Z","frame":"local metres e (east), s (south), z (elevation, MOLA datum); docs/CONTRACT.md section 1","note":"Candidate routes per scenario as planned by rl/planner.py through the engine; the stress test walks exactly these. time_s is the undisturbed walker of the stress-test simulator, engine_time_s the engine's polyline walker.","s